-- Clear 573 organisation history summaries a model wrote with no person checking them (JusticeHub, 2026-09-27).
--
-- JusticeHub's auto-approve cron (paused 2026-09-26, JusticeHub #517) copied the website-reading model's
-- history_summary onto organisation records between 20 May and 10 June whenever the model rated its own
-- confidence >= 0.95. Each summary was written from the first 4,000 characters of the organisation's
-- homepage, often page code. Checked 2026-09-27 (https://claude.ai/artifact/8NzW686QoWDxhZBvmvE5Ke):
--   - two separate readers on a random 20: 10 hold up against the organisation's own site, 4 say something
--     the site contradicts, 4 say things the site does not, 1 site changed since, 1 site did not answer;
--   - across all 592: 11 give a founding year the organisation's own site contradicts; 46 are notes about
--     the web page ("the exact founding date is not specified on the page") stored as history.
-- Ben chose to clear every summary nobody has confirmed ("clear the unchecked histories"). The 10 that both
-- readers confirmed are kept, as is any summary a person has since changed.
--
-- The text is not shown on any public JusticeHub page; it appears on admin screens and counts for 10% of
-- profile_completeness_score, so these organisations' scores drop at the next rescore.
--
-- What this does: copies (id, old value, model, cleared_at) to organizations_unchecked_histories_20260927
-- (service role only), then clears exactly those values, and ONLY where the record still holds the model's
-- text (matched by md5). Stops if the count is not exactly 573.
--
-- Apply AFTER this file is on main:
--   scripts/db-apply.sh supabase/migrations/20260927000000_clear_unchecked_org_histories.sql
-- Undo:
--   UPDATE organizations o SET history_summary = b.old_value FROM organizations_unchecked_histories_20260927 b
--    WHERE o.id = b.id AND o.history_summary IS NULL;

BEGIN;
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '30s';

